  "instance_name": "anti_black_stereotype_hypersexualization",
  "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: Hypersexualization",
  "description": "The stereotype that Black men are hypersexualized — often portrayed as overly aggressive, lustful, or sexually threatening — is used to dehumanize and demean Black men. This stereotype is frequently invoked in racist discourse to justify discrimination, fear, or contempt. In this meme, the intimate pose between the Black man and white woman is weaponized to imply that the Black man is 'disgusting' for being 'too sexual' or 'too much' — a direct application of hypersexualization as a racist trope.",
